  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison&apos;s disease): no cortisol response to cosyntropin with a markedly raised ACTH, and mineralocorticoid deficiency with raised renin and low aldosterone; on hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone; synthetic modern diagnosis chosen for a historical illness whose cause is disputed</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E27.1</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; the historical cause of her illness remains undetermined (R, disputed).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Mild normocytic anemia (hemoglobin 11.4 g/dL) with normal ferritin, vitamin B12 and folate</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D64.9</td><td>S — Synthetic finding at intake; it recovers on replacement.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

